I edited `.kiro/specs/chip-autopsy-lab/requirements.md` in place with 48 small edits, each checked to match exactly once. I also created `logs/review-requirements.md` with the 5-line log, since the file didn't exist yet. I checked the result by reading back the Stretch markers and the numbering of the edited sections; there is no test suite to run against a requirements document.

**Contradictions fixed**
- **Cause-of-death headline:** the spec said it must be a single sentence, but its own example is two sentences. It is now a fixed template, and Property 10 checks against that template. I also defined what the headline says when the lot has no failing dies.
- **Fonts:** the spec allowed JetBrains Mono and SF Pro Display, but `tech.md` self-hosts only Inter and Geist Mono. Headings now use Inter's display cut, falling back to the system SF Pro Display, and numbers use Geist Mono.
- **Pass-die colour:** `#3A4A43` on `#0A0A0B` is about 2.1:1, below the 3:1 contrast the design rules require for chart marks. It is now a starting value to tune in LCH, which is what `design-language.md` already says.
- **"Pass/fail flag invalid" bit:** dies with this `PRR` flag were all being counted as failing. They now take pass/fail from their hardware bin's pass/fail flag (`HBR.HBIN_PF`), and only count as failing, with a warning, if that is missing too.
- **URL privacy:** the URL stored the Wafer ID, a string from the STDF file, which the privacy rule forbids. It now stores a wafer index.
- **Wafer map colour cue:** a text label on every die isn't realistic at 10,000 dies. The spec now relies on pass/fail lightness contrast plus the labelled legend and hover readout.

**Untestable criteria made concrete**
- The O(1) lookup and "smoothly" wording now point to measurable targets.
- "Calibrated" confidence is impossible without labelled data in the repo, so it is now a heuristic score.
- The site-anomaly rule had only "e.g." thresholds; it now has fixed values (more than 5 percentage points below the other sites, z ≥ 3, at least 30 dies per site).
- The `None` class now uses named thresholds that `design.md` will document.
- I defined the Edge Ring Index (`edge` means the outer 3 rings) and spelled out that `Cpk` filters select tests, not dies. Property 12 now applies only to die filters.
- The probe sweep now counts inside the 3 s demo budget.
- Demo-property confidence ≥ 0.75 now applies only to the shipped demo seeds.

**Marked Stretch**
- The autopsy lamp easter egg.
- Parametric analysis of `MPR` records; they are still decoded.
- The LLM narrator and LLM translation in the Cmd-K palette, plus the server route behind them.
- Shareable URL state (all of Requirement 13).
- Loading the app with no network on first visit.
- Properties 11 and 14, and the URL part of Property 13.

All Stretch items are optional in the steering files or not mentioned there.

The performance numbers in Requirement 15 are now benchmark targets, as `tech.md` frames them. Two stay as hard pass/fail checks: no main-thread task over 50 ms during parsing, and the demo lot showing its cause of death within 3 s.

Three decisions are deferred to `design.md`:
- which verdict wins when a site problem and a spatial pattern both fire;
- the classifier's thresholds;
- the final tuned pass-die colour.[INFO] [KRS] <-- GenerateAssistantResponseCommand done totalEvents=243

